From 2e33ecccc4180a1a43c4bed0418ae4890e6f1c73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 24bit192kHz <24bit192khz@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:41:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] soc/intel/skylake: Hand the board's subsystem IDs to
 FSP

The subsystem IDs are read/write-once. FSP writes those of the PCH root
ports and of some other devices before coreboot's drivers run, so give
it the board's IDs: CONFIG_SUBSYSTEM_VENDOR_ID/DEVICE_ID if set, as
pci_dev_enable_resources() does, else the subsystemid of the system
agent in the devicetree. With neither, the values stay 0 as before.

On the other Skylake and Kaby Lake boards that have a subsystemid in
their devicetree, these devices now get the board's IDs as well.

TEST=T480 with "mb/lenovo/sklkbl_thinkpad/t480: Set the subsystem IDs"
     and CONFIG_SUBSYSTEM_* unset: the root ports, SMBus, PMC, xHCI,
     HDA and the system agent devices report 17aa:225d like the vendor
     firmware; cold boot from S5 and S3 resume with the dGPU pass.

Change-Id: Id753ed3345e888e4407733e1b7ad8718f067075d
Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: 24bit192kHz <24bit192khz@proton.me>
---
 src/soc/intel/skylake/chip.c | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/skylake/chip.c b/src/soc/intel/skylake/chip.c
index c84eb935b9..6c2f25c381 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/skylake/chip.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/skylake/chip.c
@@ -411,11 +411,20 @@ void platform_fsp_silicon_init_params_cb(FSPS_UPD *supd)
 	 */
 	params->SpiFlashCfgLockDown = lockdown_by_fsp;
 
-	/* FSP should let coreboot set subsystem IDs, which are read/write-once */
-	params->DefaultSvid = 0;
-	params->PchSubSystemVendorId = 0;
-	params->DefaultSid = 0;
-	params->PchSubSystemId = 0;
+	/*
+	 * The subsystem IDs are read/write-once. FSP writes those of the PCH
+	 * root ports and of some other devices before coreboot's drivers run,
+	 * so give it the board's IDs: from Kconfig if set, like
+	 * pci_dev_enable_resources() does, else the devicetree's subsystemid
+	 * of the system agent. Without either, they stay 0 as before.
+	 */
+	const struct device *sa = pcidev_path_on_root(SA_DEVFN_ROOT);
+	const u16 svid = CONFIG_SUBSYSTEM_VENDOR_ID ? : (sa ? sa->subsystem_vendor : 0);
+	const u16 ssid = CONFIG_SUBSYSTEM_DEVICE_ID ? : (sa ? sa->subsystem_device : 0);
+	params->DefaultSvid = svid;
+	params->PchSubSystemVendorId = svid;
+	params->DefaultSid = ssid;
+	params->PchSubSystemId = ssid;
 
 	params->PchPmWolEnableOverride = config->WakeConfigWolEnableOverride;
 	params->PchPmPcieWakeFromDeepSx = config->WakeConfigPcieWakeFromDeepSx;
